<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Buying vs Renting</span>
<h1>Long-stay Tourists: Used Motorbike Inspection for Hanoi Motorbikes</h1>
<p>The long-stay tourist who buys a used motorbike in Hanoi buys it with a countdown attached, because every month of the visit is also a month of the machine&rsquo;s life being spent on the visitor&rsquo;s tab. The inspection is the only tool that cancels the structural disadvantage of buying in an unfamiliar city, and it works at exactly one speed, slowly. This guide walks the visitor through the machine in the order that exposes expensive secrets early, invents no prices, quotes no folklore, and ends at a neutral desk where the notes can be argued before the money moves.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk maintains a rental fleet every single day and therefore knows exactly what a healthy machine sounds like, knowledge it lends freely to visitors standing in front of sellers. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-for-sale/">motorbike for sale hub</a>, study the long-stay arrangements on the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental</a> page, check the verified figures on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for maintenance and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
